<title>USA: U.S. Boxed Beef cut-out at 1500 CDT - USDA.</title>
<headline>U.S. Boxed Beef cut-out at 1500 CDT - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>DES MOINES 1997-07-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Based on FOB Omaha basis</p>
<p>carlot prices of fabricated beef cuts and on industry yields as of 1500 CDT, Boxed beef was generally steady on light to moderate demand and offerings. Select and Choice rib and round cuts steady/firm, chuck cuts weak and loin cuts firm. Beef trimmings steady on light to moderate demand and offerings.</p>
<p>  211 Fab Lds  CH 1-3	CH 1-3	SE 1-3	SE 1-3</p>
<p>   34 50s Lds 550/700     700/850     550/700     700/850</p>
<p>22 Grd Lds ---------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Values =     108.56	109.01	101.70	101.56</p>
<p>		    0.02	  0.23	  0.24	  0.22</p>
<p>Rib	  172.88	172.47	159.12	158.77</p>
<p>Chuck	 74.34	 74.57	 75.24	 73.80</p>
<p>Round	 94.45	 94.45	 91.99	 91.99</p>
<p>Loin	 170.67	172.70	146.38	147.95</p>
<p>Brisket     64.79	 64.79	 65.65	 65.65</p>
<p>Shrt Plate  67.87	 67.79	 68.12	 67.94</p>
<p>Flank	 58.13	 58.13	 58.83	 58.83</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312 408 8720))</p>
